      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T11:13:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The previous call-home node is closed before the new one is validated. If getNetconfNode() or getRemoteDeviceId() then rejects the new node, the old one is\nalready gone and nothing replaces it. Could you run both checks first and only\nthen close `prev`? For example:\n```\n  final var nodeId \u003d node.requireNodeId();\n  final var prev \u003d activeConnectors.get(nodeId);\n  if (prev instanceof NetconfNodeHandler) {\n      // WARN and return, as now\n  }\n  final var netconfNode \u003d getNetconfNode(node, nodeId);\n  if (netconfNode \u003d\u003d null) {\n      return;\n  }\n  final var deviceId \u003d getRemoteDeviceId(netconfNode, nodeId);\n  if (deviceId \u003d\u003d null) {\n      return;\n  }\n  if (prev !\u003d null) {\n      LOG.info(\"Call-home RemoteDevice{{}} was already connected, disconnecting\", nodeId);\n      activeConnectors.remove(nodeId);\n      prev.close();\n  }\n```",
      "revId": "edfa33466902bd9048caa1979d418c765a21e3e5",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
